  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Puts education as top priority with £2bn/yr funded by +1p on income tax; universal early-years places and smaller classes; substantial NHS pledges (+£540m, free eye/dental checks, cut waits); 3,000 more police; jobs and small business measures; affordable housing and ending rough sleeping; transport investment; tax and welfare reforms. TEXT_G: Calls for a national debate and a referendum on Europe; proposes a specific sovereignty-focused referendum question; urges holding it before or with the next General Election; critiques other parties for offering only a single-currency referendum.",
